; `;;` is Arturo's documentation-comment form: the interpreter reads its
; contents and stores them as function metadata for `info`. Reading it is
; the feature. Hanging on it is not.
;
; A backslash inside a `;;` comment, followed by anything that is not a
; letter, loops forever. An unbalanced `(` or `"` inside one is a syntax
; error. Neither happens with a single `;`, which is ignored outright, and
; neither needs a function anywhere near it.
;
; This header is deliberately written with single semicolons.

;; with \- dash
print "should print but never does"
